  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Each factor is \\(2\\) followed by five zeros. For multiplication with trailing zeros, multiply the nonzero parts and then append the zeros from both factors. Here \\(2\\times2=4\\), and the two factors contribute ten zeros altogether, so\n\\[\n200{,}000\\times200{,}000=40{,}000{,}000{,}000.\n\\]\nThis is forty billion, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
